/-!
# Set (e) of `A₁⁽⁶⁾`: coefficient times master, part B

For each master `I_j` of set (e) (here `I₉`, `I₁₀`, `I₁₂`, `I₁₃`, `I₁₄`, `I₁₅`, `I₁₆`, `I₁₇`, `I₁₈`;
the others are in
`QED.ThreeLoopE.SetEMastersProductsA`), with target `Lⱼ` and truncation order `pⱼ + 1`, write the
coefficient as `cⱼ = ε⁻¹ ^ pⱼ Tⱼ + ε ^ (mⱼ + 1) Qⱼ` (`QED.ThreeLoopE.setECoeffIj_eq`) and
`Lⱼ = ε⁻¹ ^ mⱼ Λⱼ` (`QED.ThreeLoopE.setELamIj`). Then
`cⱼ (Lⱼ + ε ^ (pⱼ + 1) r) = Sⱼ + ε (Aⱼ + Bⱼ r)`, where the Laurent polynomial `Sⱼ`
(`QED.ThreeLoopE.setESIj`) is the part of order `≤ 0` of `ε⁻¹ ^ pⱼ Tⱼ Lⱼ` and `Aⱼ`, `Bⱼ` are
analytic at `0` (`QED.ThreeLoopE.setECoeffIj_mul_eq`). Hence, under the input
`HasTruncLaurent f Lⱼ (pⱼ + 1)`, `cⱼ f = Sⱼ + ε g` near `0` with `g` analytic at `0`
(`QED.ThreeLoopE.setECoeffIj_mul`). The polynomials are generated by a script.
-/

@[expose] public section

open Real QED.Polylog Filter Topology QED.ThreeLoopD

namespace QED.ThreeLoopE

